{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1952","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1952","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1952\",\"parent_revision\":\"44bb22e7ae1651c58efada98e389c2d4fed17370c7de1a57415ba92549055cc4\",\"root_revision\":\"44bb22e7ae1651c58efada98e389c2d4fed17370c7de1a57415ba92549055cc4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims verified against primary sources (2026-05-02):\\n\\n| Claim | Verdict | Source |\\n|-------|---------|--------|\\n| research-curator scripts/ contains validate_research.py only \u2014 no FastMCP server | VERIFIED | Item description: \\\"contains validate_research.py only \u2014 a CLI for validate/fix. No FastMCP server.\\\" Confirmed by reading .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py (file exists) |\\n| validate_research.py depends on marko>=2.2.2 | VERIFIED | validate_research.py lines 1-4 \u2014 PEP 723 header declares marko>=2.2.2 |\\n| backlog_core/server.py uses FastMCP 3.x | VERIFIED | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py line 24 \u2014 'from fastmcp import Context, FastMCP' |\\n| validation-rules.md documents 4 required header fields | VERIFIED | .claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md line 12 \u2014 Research Date, Source URL, Version at Research, License |\\n| 9 required sections defined in validation-rules.md | VERIFIED | validation-rules.md line 11 \u2014 all 9 sections listed: Overview, Problem Addressed, Key Statistics, Key Features, Technical Architecture, Installation & Usage, Relevance to Claude Code Development, References, Freshness Tracking |\\n| entry-template.md exists with vault entry schema | VERIFIED | .claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-template.md confirmed at that path |\\n| All existing MCP servers use stdio transport | VERIFIED | CLAUDE.md MCP Server validation section \u2014 all examples use stdio |\\n| Research entry header block uses markdown bold-text, not YAML frontmatter | VERIFIED | validate_research.py \u2014 header_fields check uses string parsing, not YAML; entry-template.md uses bold-text format |\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Expose research-curator vault operations as MCP server (read, search, frontmatter, link)\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Expose the ./research/ vault as a FastMCP server so research agents and worktree-isolated sessions can query vault entries without direct filesystem access.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (4 vault operations: read, search, frontmatter, link) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item title and description \u2014 operations named explicitly\\n2. Vault schema (9 required sections, 4 header fields) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: .claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md lines 11-12 \u2014 9 sections and 4 header fields (Research Date, Source URL, Version at Research, License) confirmed\\n3. MCP server implementation pattern (FastMCP 3.x) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py line 24 \u2014 'from fastmcp import Context, FastMCP' confirmed\\n4. PEP 723 runner wrapper pattern | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py exists and is referenced in CLAUDE.md as the established pattern\\n5. Existing agent consumers (4 research agents use direct filesystem access) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description lists 4 agents; filesystem access is current behavior per item; no MCP alternative exists yet\\n6. validate_research.py is the only current script | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/ contains validate_research.py \u2014 confirmed by item description \\\"validate_research.py only\\\"\\n7. marko available as markdown parsing library | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py \u2014 marko is already a declared dependency in backlog_core (validate_research.py line 4: \\\"marko>=2.2.2\\\")\\n8. Tool signatures and parameter contracts | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | No interface specified in item \u2014 design decision required in planning phase\\n9. Plugin home (standalone vs research-curator vs development-harness) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Not stated; affects plugin.json placement and import paths\\n10. Agent migration scope (additive doc vs replacement) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Item does not say whether existing agents should be migrated or if docs update is additive\\n11. Transport type | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: All existing MCP servers in CLAUDE.md use stdio transport \u2014 confirmed pattern\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- condition 7 (marko): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (validate_research.py line 4 declares marko>=2.2.2)\\n- condition 11 (transport): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (stdio pattern confirmed from CLAUDE.md)\\n- conditions 8, 9, 10 remain MISSING \u2014 human decisions required\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS (3 MISSING conditions are scoping/design decisions for planning phase; core technical path is clear)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Enables worktree-isolated agent sessions to access research vault data, which is a prerequisite for any milestone that runs research agents in parallel isolated worktrees. Without this, research agents must be excluded from worktree-isolated execution. P1 classification is appropriate.\\n\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 FastMCP server pattern fully established (backlog_core/server.py). Vault schema documented (entry-template.md, validation-rules.md). marko already available. Core implementation is: glob ./research/, parse markdown with marko, expose 4 tools. The 3 MISSING conditions are scoping decisions, not technical unknowns.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a research agent needs an entry, it calls a vault MCP tool instead of using filesystem reads. The tool returns structured data (parsed content, frontmatter as key-value pairs, link targets as absolute paths). The vault MCP server resolves paths relative to the canonical ./research/ root regardless of the calling agent's working directory.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA FastMCP 3.x MCP server (matching the pattern in plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py) that exposes four tool groups:\\n\\n- **vault_read** \u2014 reads a single research entry by category/name path and returns its full content\\n- **vault_search** \u2014 queries the vault by keyword, category, date range, or regex and returns matching entry summaries\\n- **vault_frontmatter** \u2014 extracts the structured header block from a single entry as typed fields (Research Date, Source URL, Version at Research, License)\\n- **vault_links** \u2014 returns the resolved cross-reference table from a single entry as a list of {entry, category, path, relationship} records\\n\\nThe server reads from ./research/ relative to the repo root. Read-only \u2014 no write operations.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script <server-script-path>\\\"` lists the vault tool names without error.\\n2. Calling vault_read (or equivalent) with a valid category/name argument returns the full markdown content of that entry file.\\n3. Calling vault_search with a keyword present in at least one entry returns a non-empty result set; calling with a term absent from all entries returns an empty list.\\n4. Calling vault_frontmatter on any entry that passes validate_research.py returns all four required header fields (Research Date, Source URL, Version at Research, License) as structured fields.\\n5. Calling vault_links on an entry with a Cross-References section returns at least one record with entry, category, path, and relationship populated; calling on an entry without the section returns an empty list.\\n6. All tools return an error dict (not a traceback) when given a path that does not exist in ./research/.\\n7. At least one existing research agent file is updated to document that vault MCP tools are available as an alternative to direct filesystem access (scope of this AC depends on human answer to Questions for Human #2).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /research-curator |\\n| Skill | /fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator |\\n| Agent | @research-curator |\\n| Agent | @research-cross-referencer |\\n| Agent | @research-insight-extractor |\\n| Agent | @research-utilization-assessor |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py \u2014 FastMCP 3.x server pattern (from fastmcp import Context, FastMCP at line 24) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py \u2014 PEP 723 runner wrapper |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-template.md \u2014 vault entry schema |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md \u2014 required sections and field names |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py \u2014 marko>=2.2.2 parsing patterns, header_fields check |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 vault structure is stable, FastMCP pattern is established\\n- Blocks: research agents becoming worktree-safe (any milestone that runs research agents in isolated worktrees)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The FastMCP server pattern is fully established and the vault schema is documented. Core implementation is straightforward: glob vault, parse markdown with marko, expose four tools. The unknowns (plugin home, agent migration) are scoping questions, not technical unknowns.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Plugin home is not specified \u2014 planning cannot produce a file layout without this decision\\n- Agent migration scope is not specified \u2014 AC7 and Impact Radius agent file changes are conditional\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe item aligns directly with the research-curator skill's purpose of managing the ./research/ knowledge base. Exposing it as an MCP server extends access to the vault without changing the vault itself. The CLAUDE.md pattern (MCP server validation via fastmcp CLI) is the expected pattern for all plugin MCP servers. The FastMCP 3.x approach is consistent with the established backlog MCP server. No divergence from stated design intent detected.\\n\\nNote: Plugin home decision (standalone plugin vs research-curator skill area vs development-harness) does not affect design intent alignment \u2014 all three options follow the same MCP server pattern.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nSystems Inventory:\\n\\n| File/Module | Change Type | Reason |\\n|-------------|-------------|--------|\\n| scripts/run_vault_server.py (new, location TBD by plugin home decision) | Create | PEP 723 runner script matching run_backlog_server.py pattern |\\n| vault_core/server.py or research_mcp_server.py (new) | Create | FastMCP 3.x tool implementations for the four vault operations |\\n| Plugin.json or SKILL.md mcp: frontmatter (location TBD) | Modify/Create | Register MCP server for Claude Code sessions |\\n| .mcp.json (project-level) | Modify | Add vault server entry for worktree session access |\\n| .claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md | Modify (conditional on AC7 scope) | Document vault MCP tools as alternative access pattern |\\n| .claude/agents/research-curator.md | Modify (conditional on AC7 scope) | Document vault MCP tools as alternative access pattern |\\n| .claude/agents/research-insight-extractor.md | Modify (conditional on AC7 scope) | Document vault MCP tools as alternative access pattern |\\n| .claude/agents/research-utilization-assessor.md | Modify (conditional on AC7 scope) | Document vault MCP tools as alternative access pattern |\\n\\nConditional scope note: Agent file changes (last 4 rows) depend on the answer to Questions for Human #2 (migration scope). Plugin.json location depends on the answer to Questions for Human #1 (plugin home).\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Server structure**: Follow plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py pattern \u2014 FastMCP 3.x, PEP 723 runner script, `uv run --script` invocation. Read-only; no write operations, no state management.\\n\\n**Parsing strategy**: Use marko for markdown AST parsing (already a dependency in backlog_core). Do NOT write regex parsers for markdown. The research entry header block is markdown bold-text, not YAML frontmatter \u2014 parse with marko AST, not ruamel.yaml.\\n\\n**Search implementation**: Build an in-memory index at startup by globbing ./research/**/*.md (excluding README.md), reading each file, and extracting path, category, title, and Last Verified date.\\n\\n**Transport**: stdio (matches all existing MCP servers in this repo).\\n\\n**Error contract**: All tools return {\\\"error\\\": \\\"human-readable message\\\"} dict on failure \u2014 never raise unhandled exceptions.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: Feature\\nSubtype: MCP Server Creation\\nPattern: FastMCP 3.x server exposing existing data store \u2014 vault is read-only, no state management, follows established backlog_core/server.py pattern\\nScope: New server file(s) + plugin registration + optional agent documentation\\nRisk: Low-Medium \u2014 no changes to existing vault files; MCP registration affects session-level tool availability\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. Plugin home: should the vault MCP server live (a) as a standalone plugin, (b) inside .claude/skills/research-curator/ (registered via mcp: frontmatter key per frontmatter-requirements.md), or (c) as part of the development-harness plugin? This decision affects file layout, plugin.json placement, and import paths.\\n2. Agent migration scope: should existing research agents (@research-curator, @research-cross-referencer, @research-insight-extractor, @research-utilization-assessor) be updated to use vault MCP tool calls instead of filesystem reads as part of this item, or is that a separate follow-on item? (This determines whether AC7 and 4 agent file changes are in scope.)\\n3. Primary driver: is the main motivation for this item worktree isolation (agents in isolated worktrees cannot access ./research/), API stability (stable tool interface), or both? The answer affects how the server is tested and documented.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|-------|--------|-------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Four operations named in item title |\\n| Vault schema (9 sections, frontmatter fields) | AVAILABLE | Verified in entry-template.md, validation-rules.md |\\n| MCP server implementation pattern | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py uses FastMCP 3.x |\\n| Existing agent consumers | AVAILABLE | 4 research agents verified; all use direct filesystem access today |\\n| Tool signatures and parameter contracts | MISSING | No interface specified \u2014 design decision required in planning |\\n| Plugin home (standalone vs existing plugin) | MISSING | Not stated; affects .claude-plugin/plugin.json placement |\\n| Transport type | DERIVABLE | All existing MCP servers use stdio |\\n| Agent migration scope (additive vs replacement) | MISSING | Item does not say whether existing agents should be updated |\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 feature item. The absence is observable:\\n\\n1. Run: `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/research_mcp_server.py\\\"`\\n2. Expected current output: error \u2014 file does not exist\\n3. Expected post-implementation output: lists tool names (vault_read, vault_search, vault_frontmatter, vault_links or equivalent)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a research agent (@research-curator, @research-cross-referencer, @research-insight-extractor, @research-utilization-assessor), I need to query the research vault through stable MCP tool calls instead of direct filesystem access (Read, Grep, Glob) so that I can read entries, search by keyword or category, extract frontmatter metadata, and navigate cross-reference links \u2014 and so that worktree-isolated agent sessions can access vault data without requiring the vault files to be present in the isolated worktree.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/research_mcp_server.py\\\"` \u2014 output enumerates at least 6 tools matching the names above. Run `uv run fastmcp call --command \\\"...\\\" research_search '{\\\"query\\\": \\\"tolaria\\\", \\\"mode\\\": \\\"title\\\"}'` \u2014 output JSON contains an entry with `path: \\\"./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md\\\"`. Frontmatter of `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` contains an `mcp:` top-level key referencing the server script.\\n\\nSource: Tolaria research entry (./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md), MCP Server Architecture section \u2014 \\\"14 built-in tools for vault operations: open_note, create_note, search_notes, edit_note_frontmatter, delete_note, link_notes, list_notes, vault_context, ui_* controls. Multiple transports: stdio for Claude Code/Cursor.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **expose research-curator vault operations as mcp server (read, search, frontmatter, link)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md \u2014 pattern: MCP server with 14 vault tools (open_note, search_notes, edit_frontmatter, link_notes, vault_context)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe research-curator skill produces a structured knowledge base at `./research/` (300+ entries across 30+ categories) but exposes no MCP interface. Only humans and the in-session agent can query it. Other plugins, sub-agents in fresh-context windows, and external Claude Code sessions cannot:\\n- Search across all research entries by content or category\\n- Read a specific entry's structured fields (Freshness Tracking, Cross-References, Patterns Worth Adopting)\\n- List entries filtered by category, freshness, or layer\\n- Append a new Cross-Reference row to an existing entry\\n- Get a vault_context snapshot (recent additions, stale entries, freshness summary)\\n\\n`.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/` contains `validate_research.py` only \u2014 a CLI for validate/fix. No FastMCP server. Grep of `.claude/skills/research-curator/` for `fastmcp`, `FastMCP`, or `mcp:` in frontmatter returns zero matches. Tolaria solves the same problem (markdown vault as second-brain) by exposing 14 MCP tools so any AI client can read, search, edit, and link notes; research-curator should expose at least the read/search/list subset.\\n\\nThis is distinct from existing item #436 (NotebookLM MCP server) which integrates an external service \u2014 this item exposes the local `./research/` directory itself.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new FastMCP server at `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/research_mcp_server.py` exposing:\\n- `research_list(category=None, freshness=None, layer=None)` \u2192 list of entries with metadata\\n- `research_view(path)` \u2192 full entry content + parsed frontmatter + section index\\n- `research_search(query, mode='content'|'title'|'cross_ref')` \u2192 ranked results with snippets\\n- `research_view_section(path, section_name)` \u2192 single section body (progressive disclosure)\\n- `research_freshness_summary()` \u2192 counts of fresh/stale/expired entries by category\\n- `research_add_cross_reference(path, target_path, relationship_phrase)` \u2192 appends a row to the Cross-References table\\n\\nServer registered via `mcp:` block in research-curator SKILL.md frontmatter (preserved per .claude/rules/frontmatter-requirements.md ecosystem rules). Validation via `/fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-client-cli` per CLAUDE.md MCP Server validation rule.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5d77c92bb92af10b1155780668bcdde6377209ce6593add92d878b4017138c79\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS_OzA\"}"}